WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.480
ALL: Happy birthday to--

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.120
Take it away Amanda!

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.000
Oh, no I'm fine.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.080
Oh come on it's Sarah's birthday,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.240
let's hear you, 'Sang gurl'.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.440
Sing, Sing, Sing, Sing, Sing, Sing.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.720
Come on Beyoncé!

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.720
Happy birthday to you.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.720
CHEERING

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:22.960
That was amazing.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.080
That was so beautiful.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.960
Anyway, who wants some cake?

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.320
Yes!

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.040
It's not easy being the minority
in any situation.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.600
But in the workplace,
as the only black woman,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.480
it can be a very frustrating
and stressful environment.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.920
OK Yonce, now let's get
in formation for dis cake.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.880
I'm just in the middle of something,
I'll be there in a sec.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.840
Oh 'Okurrr!'.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.040
And that my friends is an example
of a microaggression.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.640
So what is a microaggression?

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.280
Brief, commonplace, daily verbal,
behavioural or environmental

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.560
indignities, whether intentional or
unintentional, that communicate

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.960
hostile, derogatory or negative
prejudicial slights and insults

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.000
towards any group, particularly
culturally marginalised groups.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.200
That’s right, I've read up on this.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
It felt so good to be able
to label that behaviour.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:30.000
To give a name to the underlying
stress and discomfort

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.320
that comes from being confronted
by microaggressions.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:39.200
He means well, but that's what
makes these aggressions, well, micro.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.280
Intent is not the same as impact,
and a throwaway comment or joke

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.280
can have a huge impact
on the rest of someone's day.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.520
I spoke to some friends about their
experiences in the workplace.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.760
How does it make you feel?

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.280
So we talked a lot about
these microaggressions,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.280
out-and-out racism
in the workplace,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.480
how does that make you feel?

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.760
I know that I definitely feel,

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.520
kind of, other, very separate to an
extent that I don't talk about any

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.600
kind of black experiences
I have outside of work.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.720
Some of the things that I don’t like
are those sweeping statements,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.280
'Has anybody got an umbrella? Debbie
will have one because black people

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.320
don't like to get their hair wet.'

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.440
And here is the kitchen,
where we really get things cooking.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.840
But seriously guys,
this space is used by everyone,

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.320
so just be mindful
about strong smelling foods.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.920
Right, up next, the photocopiers.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.400
I'm always super polite, super kind,
super cordial and everyone's like,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:46.600
'Oh Essi's super friendly'
but sometimes I do just want to

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.800
snap back at somebody or get
annoyed and I feel like I can't.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:54.640
I feel like the second
I display passion

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.280
for doing a good job,

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.280
people are like,
'Woah, woah, woah, woah, woah.'

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.760
That was great Amanda,

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.960
I'm not sure the figures
are quite accurate though.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.080
Actually I double-checked them
with finance to make sure

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.280
and they're spot on.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.640
Woah girlfriend, maybe
dial down the sass a little?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.080
For a lot of my white colleagues,
they're quite happy to just have

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.440
all these discussions about racism,
but because it doesn’t affect them

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.960
emotionally, whereas for me it's
quite difficult to hear those

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.440
conversations because it's like,
I have lived through a lot of that

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.000
and I'm just trying to do my work
and you're bringing up these really

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.240
difficult issues for me.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.320
Oh Amanda, thank god,
explain to Sarah what the

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.240
Black Lives Matter movement is.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.720
All jokes aside, it can be very
difficult when you find yourself

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.120
on the receiving end
of this kind of behaviour.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.600
So, what can you do about it?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.120
Well, I have a few ideas.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.200
Firstly, set up the situation.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.840
Kate, you know when you took
us on that tour the other day?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.360
Next, objectively describe the
behaviour and get clarification.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.480
You asked me to explain the
Black Lives Matter movement?

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.480
Why did you ask me?

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.440
Next, and this is the most
important bit, explain the impact.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.760
If you want the behaviour to stop,
people need to know why.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.880
John, when you use phrases like,
'Woah girlfriend' or describe me as,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.160
'Sassy', it feels like you're
accusing me of me being aggressive

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.760
and makes me worry about
sharing my opinions.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.400
I haven't seen you do this to any
other members of the team.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.800
Final step, do differently.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.200
Work together to come up with
solutions to ensure that you

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.280
do things differently in future.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.000
To be completely honest,
I hate singing on my own

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.200
and I don’t think it's fair to put
someone on the spot like that.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.400
Self-selected solos from now on?

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.080
ALL: Yeah!

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:57.520
It's not always going to be that
easy, but hopefully these tips will

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.720
provide some helpful navigation
through difficult situations.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.160
And if don’t improve
or if you don’t feel comfortable

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.600
confronting a colleague,
talk to your boss, HR or union rep.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.520
Racial discrimination
at work is illegal.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:16.000
It's everyone's responsibility
to think about the impact

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.200
that their words might
have on someone else.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:22.760
Now, if you don’t mind,
I've got a party to get back to.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.800
Who's for cake?

